{
	"name": "Paper Beast",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/sundries/documents/blueprint-recipe-alchemical.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Tiny constructs made entirely out of parchment, paper beasts often arise out of artists’ studios or wizards’ laboratories— any place where paper is frequently crumpled and tossed. A DC 12 Arcana check reveals that paper beasts come to life from the coalescence of many discarded ideas or abandoned projects, spontaneously granting the paper life. What form they take may vary, from a delicate crane to a paper dragon, though its shape is almost always related to the personality that created it.</p><p>Discarded ideas still hold power, however, even if they were abandoned. If adventurers attempt to perform the Craft, Research, or Spellcraft downtime activities while in the presence of a paper beast, they gain an expertise die to the relevant roll.</p><p>Paper beasts are inexorably tied to the place of their creation, however, and cannot be removed. Any paper beast that is taken out of its point of origin immediately loses its magic and reverts back to a pile of discarded paper.</p>",
